{
  "dom_id": "step-q96413",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{2}+1}{{3}^{2}-1}+\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
